# CAMPUSBITE
## Restaurant Ordering & Delivery Platform
**Project Documentation**

---

## 1. Introduction

CampusBite is a full-stack restaurant ordering and delivery platform developed to simplify the process of ordering food online and managing restaurant operations.

The platform provides a common system for customers, restaurant owners and delivery partners. Customers can explore restaurants, browse food menus, place orders and track their order status. Restaurant owners can manage restaurant details, menu items and incoming orders, while delivery partners can view assigned deliveries and update their delivery progress.

The application integrates frontend development, backend API services and relational database management to provide a centralized food ordering solution.

## 2. Problem Statement

Traditional food ordering and restaurant management processes can involve manual communication, difficulty managing orders and limited visibility into delivery progress.

Customers may find it difficult to track their orders, while restaurant owners need an organized way to manage menus and incoming orders. Delivery partners also require access to their assigned orders and delivery information.

CampusBite aims to address these challenges by providing a centralized digital platform that connects all three user roles and simplifies the overall ordering and delivery process.

## 3. Project Objectives

The main objectives of CampusBite are:

- To develop a user-friendly online restaurant ordering platform.
- To allow customers to browse restaurants and explore available food items.
- To provide customers with the ability to place orders and monitor order progress.
- To enable restaurant owners to manage menus, restaurant information and incoming orders.
- To allow delivery partners to access assigned deliveries and update their status.
- To maintain application data using a structured relational database.
- To implement secure user authentication and role-based access.
- To develop and run the application using Docker containerization.

